#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""supernote: let an agent control a Supernote e-ink tablet over Wi-Fi ADB with direct calls, JSON answers and stable exit codes, without root.

Direct calls come first (intents, content providers, files), then element references from a
snapshot, and coordinates only as the last resort. Every command takes --json.

  status                         connection, firmware, screen size, battery, foreground activity
  firmware [--download]          show the installed and newest official firmware; --download copies it to EXPORT
  routes [PACKAGE]               list, read-only, the device's entry points and which job each one does
  doctor                         check, read-only, that each call this command makes still exists
  note open PATH [--page N]      open a note; N counts from 1, as the device shows it
  note new PATH                  create a blank portrait note at PATH and open it; never replaces
  files ls [PATH]                list a folder of the shared storage
  files pull PATH LOCAL          copy from the shared storage
  files push LOCAL PATH          copy to the shared storage; refuses to replace without --overwrite
  sync tasks                     start a To-do sync and wait until it has run
  sync calendar                  ask the Calendar app to sync
  screen FILE.png                save what the screen shows
  snapshot                       list the screen's elements with short references;
                                 --all reads each list to its end, --find X scrolls to an element
  click TARGET                   press an element: @eN from the last snapshot, id:X, desc:X, text:X
  wait activity|file|element X   wait for a condition instead of sleeping (--timeout SECONDS)
  apps                           installed packages
  plugin ls                      installed plugins
  plugin push FILE.snplg         copy a plugin to MyStyle; the install is then done on the device
  plugin install FILE.snplg      copy, install or update through named elements, and prove it
  logs [--tag T] [--lines N]     recent device log, with credentials masked; see logs --help for
                                 --level, --package, --pid, --grep, --since, --since-last,
                                 --follow and --plugin
  history                        what this command did: --failures, --command NAME, --since 2h
  tap X Y | swipe X1 Y1 X2 Y2    press by coordinates, the last resort
  wifi off                       turn Wi-Fi ADB off when the work ends, and say how to turn it on
  shell COMMAND...               run a command on the device

click, tap, swipe and note accept --snapshot (add a fresh snapshot to the result) and --screen FILE
(save a fresh capture), so one call shows its effect.

--read-only, or $SUPERNOTE_READ_ONLY, refuses every command that changes the device.
--allow-notes lets files pull and screen read the notes folder or a note on the screen.
--trace prints each ADB call to stderr as it runs. --log-paths also keeps full call arguments.

The device's address is $SUPERNOTE_ADDRESS, else the first line of
~/.config/supernote-adb/address, as HOST or HOST:PORT. PATH is relative to the shared storage, or absolute.
ADB over Wi-Fi is enabled once over USB with `adb tcpip 5555`; a restart of the device turns it off.
"""

